Structured RAG Retrieval Pipeline (Natural Language to SQL)
This project implements the Retrieve phase of a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture. It allows users to query a relational SQLite database (hotels.db) using natural language, automatically translates those requests into validated SQL statements, and safely executes them to return results as a Pandas DataFrame.

Features
Schema-Aware Query Generation: Uses LangChain prompt templates combined with the database schema and 3 sample rows to help the LLM generate accurate, context-aware SQLite statements.

Pipeline Cleaning & Sanitization (clean_sql): Extracts the raw SQL text string from LangChain's AIMessage object and strips out markdown code block fences (```sql).

Security Firewall (validate_sql): Inspects the generated SQL query for dangerous operations (DROP, DELETE, TRUNCATE, ALTER, CREATE, INSERT, UPDATE) to protect the underlying database.

Execution & DataFrame Conversion (execute_sql): Safely connects to the SQLite database via Pandas and sqlite3 to fetch matching records.

LangChain Expression Language (LCEL): Chains the components together cleanly using the pipe operator (|):

